{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 28, :comments ["<b>We have surely seen.</b> We saw when you stayed in Gerar that the land was blessed with a hundredfold, and we saw now, after you left there, that its blessing ceased from it, and the matter depends only on you, for HaShem was with you." "<b>Between us, between us and you. Between us</b> — the oath that we shall swear in our fear now as well; <b>between us and you</b> — that you too shall swear by them." "<b>And let a covenant be cut with you.</b> Even though Abraham and Avimelech had already sworn up to three generations, in any case Avimelech sought to cut a new covenant between them, because he had breached the covenant regarding the wells and regarding that they sent him away from him."], :book :genesis, :voice :chizkuni, :lang :en, :chapter 26, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-30T15:06:08.377762565Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}